# Notion Comments Polish: Persistence, Interaction & Auto-Hide Walkthrough

We have successfully resolved the comments saving issues, retired `localStorage` in favor of direct database payload syncing, fixed the popover item selection and file uploading interactions, and added a premium auto-hide feature with a configuration settings dropdown in the header.

## Changes Made

### 1. Database Persistence Fix
- **File**: [notionPageDefaults.ts](file:///c:/BriselleServer/Briselle-Lightiningv58/briselle-lightining.client/src/modules/notion-nest/notionPageDefaults.ts#L200-L215)
  - Fixed `parseNotionPageFromValues` to map and parse the `comments` property from the database record payload. Previously, reloading the page wiped out comments because the parser ignored this field.
- **File**: [PageContext.jsx](file:///c:/BriselleServer/Briselle-Lightiningv58/briselle-lightining.client/src/modules/notion-nest/PageContext.jsx#L35-L48)
  - Disabled `localStorage` checks/saves on comment initialization and operations. All changes now flow exclusively through page state updates and save to the database.
  - Added a `useEffect` hook to keep local comments synchronized with `initialComments` updates.

### 2. Interaction & Focus Management in Popovers
- **File**: [menus.jsx](file:///c:/BriselleServer/Briselle-Lightiningv58/briselle-lightining.client/src/modules/notion-nest/menus.jsx#L867-L958)
  - **Attachment Popover**: Removed `e.preventDefault()` from the parent wrapper's `onMouseDown` handler. This 
